# Anything that is not part of the addon itself stays out of the repo: working
# notes, tool output, editor and assistant state. A plain clone into
# Interface\AddOns should contain exactly what the game loads, plus the tests
# and the public README.

# assistant / editor state
.claude/

# knowledge graph output -- generated, and belongs under D:\Graphify\
graphify-out/

# session handover notes: local working document, full of absolute paths
HANDOFF.md

# session status notes: local working doc, same reason as HANDOFF.md
STATUS.md

# a patch against Nampower's C++ source, not part of what the game loads. It is
# a note about a possible client change, and shipping it in an addon folder
# invites somebody to think the addon needs a custom Nampower build. It does
# not -- the yardage ladder works on a stock one.
native/
